I also had the problem that I can't see any walls in your replays O.o,
which is inconvenient to say the least :)

In general I have to say, that my enthusiasm to watch tournament
replays is now a bit limited, as I discovered several things about
them:
- As mentioned above the "best behaved" ones (also the one from rax,
where I gave up as well) are pretty long, though most interesting from
a gameplay perspective. But I think a YAAP is far better suited than
watching hours over hours of ttyrecs, even with 4xLog speed you end up
missing the important pieces anyways :)
- The early and mid game of "fasttest" ascensions turn out to be
rather boring, as most of the time the player was just lucky with
wishes or randomly generated items and I totally forgot about bone
files... which screw such things totally up anyways. I think most of
these games "just happened" to be fast, it wasn't planned from
character creation to go for that trophy. But I don't want to raise a
new conduct etc. discussion again, I just mean the interesting part of
such replays reduces to how the later game (from castle onward) is
sped up.

I think I might be a bit restricted with what games I'd value to see
and the tourney games might not be the right source for them.
Especially when conducts are involved I'd like to see how people solve
the problem without using bone files. Early wands of wishing might
also turn out to be not that interesting, depending on how early they
are found I guess. I mean a certain number of wishes is certainly
nothing uncommon, so a (0:1) wand and no magic lamps in the mines
might be worthwhile again :)

Maybe I give other trophies a try, like the "truest pacifist" one,
that might turn out to be interesting.

